<Project>

  <!--
    Vixen — the synthetic project generator of docs/plan/12 § "Test infrastructure worth building
    early", linked rather than referenced, on the same argument as Vixen.Testing.props beside it.

    ITS OWN FILE, like GoldenFile's and TestApp's, and here the reason is what the file NEEDS rather
    than only what it is for: FixtureProject writes real assets, so it names PngCodec out of
    Vixen.Core.Imaging. Linking it into a test project with no imaging reference is a build error in
    return for nothing.

    Consumers need a `using Vixen.Testing;` and a reference that brings in Vixen.Core.Imaging —
    which anything importing a texture already has. Unlike the other three it names no test
    framework at all: a fixture on disk is a fixture on disk, and its refusals are exceptions rather
    than assertions so that the failure arrives before the test does.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)FixtureProject.cs" Link="Testing\FixtureProject.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
